// child/sandbox/boot-consolidation/prompt-sync/M4_prompt_sync.vsm
// PROPOSAL M4 (design only — target .opencode/agent/vsf-s3-planner.md would
// be EDITED in production only after parent acceptance. This document is
// the exact replacement text.)
//
// Spec source: boot_ontology_pattern.vsm §6 R_D2 + §7 D_PROMPT_SYNC + P3
// (role-operates: the prompt lists the ROLE's operational boot tail, does
// NOT re-state canon order).
// Current file read read-only: .opencode/agent/vsf-s3-planner.md lines
// 13-29 (Boot section). Line 19-24 re-lists the six boot docs (D1/D2).
// Line 27-28 boot tail = HANDOFF + TASKS (omits onboard.sh — D2).

proposal("M4-PROMPT-SYNC") {

  // ════ WHAT CHANGES ════
  what: "The Boot section of vsf-s3-planner.md stops re-listing the six boot
      docs (D1) and cites the manifest as the index (P4). The role's
      operational boot tail (HANDOFF, TASKS) stays; onboard.sh is ADDED to
      the tail (closes D2 — S3 must observe reality before planning, per the
      agent_loop OBSERVE phase).",

  // ════ EXACT REPLACEMENT — the whole Boot section (lines 13-29) ════
  replacement: "
    ## Boot — read in this order, always (clean or post-compact)

    Compaction summary is RECALL, not canon: every claim is a lead to verify,
    never a fact. Read first:

    ```
    1. docs/spec_revision/system/boot/boot_manifest.vsm — the boot index:
       every artifact the boot loads, by layer, with role and hash. Follow
       it; do not improvise the order (R5).
    2. RULES.md            — hard rules (injected by opencode.json; canon is
                              hard_rules.vsm)
    3. HANDOFF.vsm.md      — actual current state
    4. TASKS.vsm (end)     — last session block + open tasks
    5. bash scripts/state/onboard.sh — reality contact (state_query focus +
       live state), then plan.
    ```
    The six boot docs (covenant ≻ core_boot_primer ≻ vsl_language_primer ≻
    regulation_layer ≻ hard_rules ≻ communication_protocol) are the canon;
    the manifest lists them with their hashes. Read the docs themselves from
    the manifest on demand (dependency order is in the manifest, not
    re-listed here — P3).",
  replacement_note: "the replacement REMOVES the verbatim 'ALL 6 (VSL boot
      package)' re-listing (currently lines 19-24) and replaces it with the
      manifest citation + onboard.sh in the tail. The dependency-order
      sentence becomes a single normative pointer (P1/P4).",

  // ════ WHY THIS TEXT (vs alternatives) ════
  decisions: [
    "D1: onboard.sh added to the TAIL (step 5) not the top — R5 canon first,
        then role state, then reality contact (matches agent_loop
        BOOT→OBSERVE). This closes D2 (the omission) without reordering the
        canon-first boot.",
    "D2: 'the manifest lists them with their hashes' — the prompt CITES the
        manifest (P4), it does not copy the list. The parent's R_D2 offered
        'prompt gains onboard.sh OR reminder sole owner' — this proposal
        takes the FIRST option (add onboard.sh) + manifest-as-index, because
        the reminder is advisory and the prompt is the operating layer (P3).",
    "D3: no other section of vsf-s3-planner.md changes (verified read-only:
        capabilities, supervision, deploy pattern, verification, session
        close, command chain are not boot-order text).",
  ],

  // ════ VERIFY PLAN ════
  verify_plan: "boot load test: new S3 session starts, reads manifest,
      reminder fires, verifier advisory passes, within token budget.
      M2 check (c): prompt's citations resolve (manifest exists).",

  // ════ RISK ════
  risk: "LOW — prompt edit (migration M4, §9). Rollback: single commit.",
}
⟦ /m4_prompt_sync ⟧